{title: Blind in the Light}
{subtitle: Acts 13:6–7; 13:7–8; 13:9–10; 13:11; 13:12}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] |
| [Dm] | [Gm7] | [Em7b5] | [A7] | ×2

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dm7]They traveled through the is[Gm7]land to Pa[C7]phos
Found a Jewish ma[Fmaj7]gician [Bbmaj7]and false prophet
Named Bar-Je-sus [Gm7]with the procon[A7]sul
Sergius Paulus an [Dm]in[Dm7/C]telli[Bbmaj7]gent man
The proconsul sent for Barna[Gm7]bas and [A7]Saul
Eager to hear the [Dm]word [Dm7]of God
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
You are full of [Gm7]every kind of [C7]deceit
You son [Fmaj7]of the devil [Bbmaj7]and fraud
En[Bbmaj7/A]emy of [Gm7]all that is right
[A7]Twisting the straight paths of the [Dm]Lord
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[A7]But E[Dm]lymas the magician opposed [Gm7]them
[C7]Trying to turn the proconsul a[Fmaj7]way
[Fmaj7/A]From the [Bbmaj7]faith he sought [Bbmaj7/A]to [Gm7]find
Saul looked [A7]straight at him with power
Filled with the Holy Spirit in that [Dm]moment
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
You are full of every kind [Gm7]of deceit
[C7]You son of the [Fmaj7]devil and fraud
[Bbmaj7]Enemy [Dm7/A]of all [Gm7]that is right
[A7]Twisting the straight paths of the [Dm]Lord
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Dm7/C]The [Bbmaj7]hand of the Lord is against you
[Gm7]You will be blind and [C7]unable to see
A mist [Fmaj7]and [Bbmaj7]darkness came over [Gm7]him
He groped a[A7]bout seeking a hand to lead
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
When the proconsul saw what had hap[Dm]pened
He believed as[A7]tounded at the teach[Dm]ing
{end_of_verse}

